{"abstract":"POPLMark and POPLMark Reloaded sparked a flurry of work on machine-checked proofs, and fostered the adoption of proof mechanisation in programming language research. Both challenges were purposely limited in scope, and they do not address concurrency-related issues. We propose a new collection of benchmark challenges focused on the difficulties that typically arise when mechanising formal models of concurrent and distributed programming languages, such as process calculi. Our benchmark challenges address three key topics: linearity, scope extrusion, and coinductive reasoning. The goal of this new benchmark is to clarify, compare, and advance the state of the art, fostering the adoption of proof mechanisation in future research on concurrency.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Carbone, Marco","Castro-Perez, David","Ferreira, Francisco","Gheri, Lorenzo","Jacobsen, Frederik Krogsdal","Momigliano, Alberto","Padovani, Luca","Scalas, Alceste","Tirore, Dawit","Vassor, Martin","Yoshida, Nobuko","Zackon, Daniel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747145"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-21","place":"Groningen, nl","start":"2024-06-17","title":"26th International Conference on Coordination Models and Languages","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jacobsen, Frederik Krogsdal"],"country":["Canada","Italy","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","McGill University","University of Kent","University of Liverpool","University of London","University of Oxford","Università degli Studi di Milano-Bicocca","Università di Camerino"],"keyword":["Benchmark","Coinduction","Linearity","Mechanisation","Process calculi"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the concurrent calculi formalisation benchmark","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85197262235","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747145","identifier":[{"id":"85197262235","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ed981072-6e7b-4059-9ad4-f0aa3e5077e3"],"keyword":["Benchmark","Coinduction","Linearity","Mechanisation","Process calculi","Scope extrusion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BD52CF619AD4BC41F812EE5263EB6F15"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of kent","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Kent","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of London","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of liverpool","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Liverpool","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Algorithms, Logic and Graphs"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"it","key":"università degli studi di milano bicocca","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Università degli Studi di Milano-Bicocca","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"it","key":"università di camerino","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Università di Camerino","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"ca","key":"mcgill university","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"McGill University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","name":"Carbone, Marco","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"castroperezpau","last":"Castro-Perez","name":"Castro-Perez, David","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Francisco","key":"ferreirapau","last":"Ferreira","name":"Ferreira, Francisco","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lorenzo","key":"gheripau","last":"Gheri","name":"Gheri, Lorenzo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederik Krogsdal","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"8ccfbd6a-fd5f-4b82-b2e9-2c367460abf8","name":"Jacobsen, Frederik Krogsdal","orcid":"0000-0003-3651-8314","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Alberto","key":"momiglianopau","last":"Momigliano","name":"Momigliano, Alberto","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Luca","key":"padovanipau","last":"Padovani","name":"Padovani, Luca","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Alceste","key":"scalaspau","last":"Scalas","locid":"52ce37f8-955f-4a14-b8ed-c59dc660bfc0","name":"Scalas, Alceste","orcid":"0000-0002-1153-6164","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dawit","key":"tirorepau","last":"Tirore","name":"Tirore, Dawit","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"vassorpau","last":"Vassor","name":"Vassor, Martin","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Nobuko","key":"yoshidapau","last":"Yoshida","name":"Yoshida, Nobuko","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel","key":"zackonpau","last":"Zackon","name":"Zackon, Daniel","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-62697-5_9","eisbn":["9783031626975"],"isbn":["9783031626968"],"pages":"149-158","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of 26th International Conference on Coordination Models and Languages","volume":"14676"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85197262235"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ed981072-6e7b-4059-9ad4-f0aa3e5077e3"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"The Concurrent Calculi Formalisation Benchmark","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747145","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In the modern age of computing, distributed systems are ubiquitous. Besides the positive aspects of distributed systems, such as their scalability, they remain hard to implement due to the intricacies of parallel execution. A type discipline known as session types offers an appealing theoretical foundation for verifying the correctness of distributed systems. Session types are increasingly used in practice, seen by its integration into many mainstream programming languages and the emergence of standalone session type based tools, making it increasingly important to verify its theoretical foundations. Guarantees offered by session types rely on formal proofs, and errors in these proofs have been uncovered in multiple heavily cited session type papers, and this has motivated the use of proof assistants to verify results within the field. Mechanised results exist for the restricted formalism called binary session types, supporting the verification of two communicating roles. Mechanised results for the more expressive multiparty session types, allowing an arbitrary number of roles, is however far more limited. In particular, the claims of the original paper by Honda et al, who introduced multiparty session types more than a decade ago, remain unverified. This thesis addresses this problem by providing a faithful mechanisation of results from Honda et al.. The contributions are twofold. Our first contribution is a novel definition of the critical procedure of multiparty session types known as projection, extending on prior results by proving our definition not only sound, as others have for other formulations, but also complete, doing so against a coinductive specification of projection. Our second contribution is that we identify a counterexample to the subject reduction theorem of Honda et al., and we define a new type system that addresses this counterexample, and mechanise a subject reduction theorem for this type system. Designed with decidability in mind, we provide decision procedures for several of the properties the type system relies on.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Tirore, Dawit"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798552"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a mechanisation of multiparty session types","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"do","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://en.itu.dk/-/media/EN/Research/PhD-Programme/PhD-defences/2024/Thesis_Temporary_version_Dawit_Tirore-pdf.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798552","ids":["itu-a934d36b-f7e4-404a-bd3a-fa1cbda10b15"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1692ACA0EEEC2AD0E5B0B2C09F75FB15"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dawit","key":"tirorepau","last":"Tirore","locid":"12df9187-47b5-4d7e-87f5-9089a3d229c1","name":"Tirore, Dawit","orcid":"0000-0002-1997-5161","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16023536"],"issue":"231","pages":"160","publisher":"IT-Universitetet i København","series":"ITU-DS","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a934d36b-f7e4-404a-bd3a-fa1cbda10b15"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Mechanisation of Multiparty Session Types","type":"Other","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798552","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Multiparty session types is a typing discipline used to write specifications, known as global types, for branching and recursive message-passing systems. A necessary operation on global types is projection to abstractions of local behaviour, called local types. Typically, this is a computable partial function that given a global type and a role erases all details irrelevant to this role. Computable projection functions in the literature are either unsound or too restrictive when dealing with recursion and branching. Recent work has taken a more general approach to projection defining it as a coinductive, but not computable, relation. Our work defines a new computable projection function that is sound and complete with respect to its coinductive counterpart and, hence, equally expressive. All results have been mechanised in the Coq proof assistant.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Tirore, Dawit","Bengtson, Jesper","Carbone, Marco"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695307"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Coq","Mechanisation","Projection","Session types"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a sound and complete projection for global types","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/opus/volltexte/2023/18403/pdf/LIPIcs-ITP-2023-28.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695307","identifier":[{"id":"85168768440","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ed2c6e7a-d23b-4243-8a79-703d470a4895"],"keyword":["Coq","Mechanisation","Projection","Session types"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-5CCB516C5885FDDD1B2BA73762D97C9B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/opus/volltexte/2023/18403/pdf/LIPIcs-ITP-2023-28.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/opus/volltexte/2023/18403/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dawit","key":"tirorepau","last":"Tirore","locid":"12df9187-47b5-4d7e-87f5-9089a3d229c1","name":"Tirore, Dawit","orcid":"0000-0002-1997-5161","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"bengtsonpau","last":"Bengtson","locid":"b2b68ce2-6257-45bf-ab48-dc17d05c885e","name":"Bengtson, Jesper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","locid":"9027b41a-4159-4db7-9ddd-8fc8f41f1fb3","name":"Carbone, Marco","orcid":"0000-0001-9479-2632","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["18688969"],"journal":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik GmbH","status":"p","title":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","volume":"268"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85168768440"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ed2c6e7a-d23b-4243-8a79-703d470a4895"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Sound and Complete Projection for Global Types","type